{"agent":"bfix-lane9","data":{"by":"Qwen/Qwen3.8-Flash-Next-FP8","evidence":{"chunk_findings":[{"chunk":1,"detail":"This test is not a real regression guard for `test_every_extra_has_a_contract`: it only checks a locally constructed set against the global `_EXTRA_IMPORTS`, never pyproject or the actual contract test. If `numpy` is later added as a legitimate optional dependency (add `numpy` to `_EXTRA_IMPORTS` and to `forbidden_modules` so the contract test passes), this test fails because `dists - set(_EXTRA_IMPORTS)` no longer contains `numpy`. Conversely, if `test_every_extra_has_a_contract` is reverted to the old hard-coded extra-name check while `_EXTRA_IMPORTS` and `_dist_name` remain, this test still passes, so it does not prevent the original bug from returning.","digest":"4d947aadaacf8fbb","location":"tests/test_architecture_import_contracts.py:test_package_added_under_existing_extra_is_checked","severity":"MEDIUM","title":"tests/test_architecture_import_contracts.py:test_package_added_under_existing_extra_is_checked"},{"chunk":1,"detail":"`_dist_name` omits `@` from the separator regex, but PEP 508 also supports direct-reference requirements such as `name@url`. Given a pyproject optional dependency like `mcp@https://example.com/mcp-1.0.tar.gz`, `_dist_name` returns the whole string (or a wrong prefix if the URL contains `=`, `[`, `;`, etc.), so `dists` mismatches `_EXTRA_IMPORTS` and `test_every_extra_has_a_contract` fails/misclassifies the package even though its distribution name is `mcp`.","digest":"b79089ca6231996d","location":"tests/test_architecture_import_contracts.py:_dist_name","severity":"LOW","title":"tests/test_architecture_import_contracts.py:_dist_name"},{"chunk":1,"detail":"The new “regression” test never invokes `test_every_extra_has_a_contract` or `_contracts()`. It only builds a local `extras` dict and asserts that `\"numpy\"` is absent from `_EXTRA_IMPORTS`. In an environment where the actual guard is reverted to the old hard-coded `_EXTRA_MODULES` behavior while `_EXTRA_IMPORTS` remains as-is, this test still passes, so it does not actually detect the B-arch-guard-extras-hardcoded regression it claims to cover.","digest":"64e50b00a15c8c31","location":"tests/test_architecture_import_contracts.py:test_package_added_under_existing_extra_is_checked","severity":"MEDIUM","title":"tests/test_architecture_import_contracts.py:test_package_added_under_existing_extra_is_checked"},{"chunk":1,"detail":"The regression test hard-codes `numpy` as the “undeclared” package, so it can fail even when the guard is working correctly. If `numpy` is later added as a legitimate optional dependency and the contract is updated properly (`_EXTRA_IMPORTS[\"numpy\"] = \"numpy\"` and `numpy` included in `extras-one-adapter`’s `forbidden_modules`), then `_undeclared_imports({\"rag\": [\"model2vec>=0.9.0\", \"numpy>=1.26\"]})` returns `{}` and the assertion `problems == {\"numpy\": None}` fails. The same exact-equality check also fails if `numpy` is only partially updated (e.g. mapped but not forbidden, returning `{\"numpy\": \"numpy\"}`), making the test brittle against valid dependency/contract changes rather than isolating the regression logic.","digest":"3744724a649cb32c","location":"tests/test_architecture_import_contracts.py:test_package_added_under_existing_extra_is_checked","severity":"MEDIUM","title":"tests/test_architecture_import_contracts.py:test_package_added_under_existing_extra_is_checked"},{"chunk":1,"detail":"The regression test hard-codes `numpy` as the undeclared package and asserts the exact result `{\"numpy\": None}`. When `numpy` is later legitimately added to `_EXTRA_IMPORTS` and to the `forbidden_modules` contract (a valid architecture change), `_undeclared_imports({\"rag\": [\"model2vec>=0.9.0\", \"numpy>=1.26\"]})` returns `{}`, so the assertion fails even though the guard is correct. This is a false-positive for a future permitted dependency; use a synthetic package name or monkeypatch the maps.","digest":"5994a2070248dbe3","location":"tests/test_architecture_import_contracts.py:test_package_added_under_existing_extra_is_checked","severity":"MEDIUM","title":"tests/test_architecture_import_contracts.py:test_package_added_under_existing_extra_is_checked"},{"chunk":1,"detail":"It still does not invoke the function that had the regression, `test_every_extra_has_a_contract`; it calls the new helper `_undeclared_imports` directly. If a future edit restores the old hard-coded `_EXTRA_MODULES` behavior in `test_every_extra_has_a_contract` while leaving `_undeclared_imports` intact, this regression test passes, so it fails to detect the exact regression it is named for.","digest":"24867c0817cfc3b6","location":"tests/test_architecture_import_contracts.py:test_package_added_under_existing_extra_is_checked","severity":"LOW","title":"tests/test_architecture_import_contracts.py:test_package_added_under_existing_extra_is_checked"},{"chunk":1,"detail":"The previous `dists == set(_EXTRA_IMPORTS)` check was dropped. Given a pyproject where a package is removed from all extras while its `_EXTRA_IMPORTS` entry remains (e.g., `model2vec` removed but still mapped), `_undeclared_imports` iterates only `extras.values()` and therefore returns `{}`; `test_every_extra_has_a_contract` passes with a stale import map that the old guard caught.","digest":"508101307a4313e8","location":"tests/test_architecture_import_contracts.py:_undeclared_imports","severity":"LOW","title":"tests/test_architecture_import_contracts.py:_undeclared_imports"}],"chunks_total":1,"coverage":"1/1 chunk(s) reviewed","delta_findings":4,"delta_from":"a641ac6e35e58f8262e3161f8b4f21ce3f6b29ff","delta_raised":["3744724a649cb32c","5994a2070248dbe3","24867c0817cfc3b6","508101307a4313e8"],"delta_rounds":1,"diff_chars":3958,"diff_sha":"18f61fae5a26f2f9175ca36985c9ee96823619602581be5497e85e3fa4fc6fd8","diff_source":"delta review of 1 commit since a641ac6e35","diff_stat":{"deletions":0,"files":0,"insertions":0,"untracked":0},"elapsed_s":134.6,"family":"alibaba","findings":7,"full_coverage":"1/1 chunk(s) reviewed","max_chunk_chars":5000,"model":"Qwen/Qwen3.8-Flash-Next-FP8","output_digest":"934643b2cb2c17d2","output_file":".ddflow/local/reviews/fix-B-arch-guard-extras-hardcoded.rubber_duck.qwen3.8-flash-next-fp8.20261102T220932Z-aa2f3eeb.jsonl","reason":"","review_kind":"delta","reviewed":[1],"reviewed_head":"479df78ea366e103c583e9a0247cfc319488da5a","reviewed_paths":{"tests/test_architecture_import_contracts.py":"100644 a3641e1bad6a2296f51fb978311f34963b679ab9"},"reviewer":"qwen3.8-flash-next-fp8","reviewer_digest":"3926c0df5644d7de","rounds":1,"status":"REVIEWED","titles":["tests/test_architecture_import_contracts.py:test_package_added_under_existing_extra_is_checked","tests/test_architecture_import_contracts.py:_dist_name","tests/test_architecture_import_contracts.py:test_package_added_under_existing_extra_is_checked","tests/test_architecture_import_contracts.py:test_package_added_under_existing_extra_is_checked","tests/test_architecture_import_contracts.py:test_package_added_under_existing_extra_is_checked","tests/test_architecture_import_contracts.py:test_package_added_under_existing_extra_is_checked","tests/test_architecture_import_contracts.py:_undeclared_imports"],"tree_sha":"479df78ea366+clean","unreviewed":[],"waves":1},"gate":"rubber_duck","reason":"4 finding(s)"},"id":"e87f93f3e863edce074e859be","kind":"gate.failed","lamport":130194,"schema":1,"subject":"fix-B-arch-guard-extras-hardcoded","ts":"2026-11-02T22:17:31.658127Z"}
